// spec: TYP-013
//
// A type name must denote a declared type.  A name that denotes nothing is
// refused when the program is read, rather than being read as a type no value
// has.
//
// ⚠️ This used to be silently false, so a misspelled type answered false and
// the branch it guarded never ran -- 'if X is Integr then' took the else arm
// for every X and the program reported success.  The same undefined name used
// as a VALUE has always been 'Undefined variable', so 'is' was uniquely
// permissive about its right-hand side.

WriteLn (1 is Nonexistent);
